Package: gpuwho
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34)
Recommends: nvidia-persistenced
Description: who is using the GPUs, when one frees up, and who used how much
 gpuwho is a single-binary tool for shared GPU servers.  It answers three
 questions: who is on the GPUs right now, when a GPU will become free, and who
 used how much over a given period.
 .
 The snapshot and wait commands query the driver on demand and need nothing
 running in the background.  History is an optional layer on top: the driver's
 accounting mode, a systemd timer running a one-shot collector, and an
 append-only event log that reports are computed from.
 .
 It links against libnvidia-ml, the library behind nvidia-smi, rather than
 parsing nvidia-smi output, and reads /proc for the parts NVML does not know
 about, such as who owns a pid.  Only compute contexts are counted; graphics
 processes such as Xorg and the desktop session are excluded by construction.
 .
 This package requires an installed NVIDIA driver, which provides
 libnvidia-ml.so.1 at run time.  Driver packages vary by vendor and version, so
 that is not expressed as a hard dependency here.
